to-be-incorporated-into-paper-source = lines-of (cons "**To check against the paper (the value `hyperactivity`, `docs/hyperactivity.cub`; its Part I is v31's text, 14 November 2026): this file was written against the 11 November copy; whatever v31 already contains leaves it (Avik, 2026-11-14: done when it matters).**" (cons "" (cons "# To be incorporated into the paper" (cons "" (cons "The paper is the specification of hyperactivity. It is one value of the language, `hyperactivity`" (cons "(`docs/hyperactivity.cub`), version 32, 15 November 2026. This file is the scratch space for everything that belongs in the" (cons "paper and is not yet in that value: it is read together with the" (cons "paper, and an agent working on the paper or the code holds both. When a draft absorbs a part of" (cons "this file, that part leaves it." (cons "" (cons "## What hyperactivity is for" (cons "" (cons "**Knowledge is a lack of ignorance** (Avik, 2026-11-15 09:55 UTC). All historically separate" (cons "distinctions fail to be primitive. The primitive is provided: it supports analysis over any cut," (cons "requires no cut, and proves the bounds of analysis of all cuts. Knowledge is not to be divided into" (cons "domains; domains are bubbles of people who choose the same set of ignorances. The process that makes" (cons "them is not a knowledge process but an ignorance process." (cons "" (cons "**Controversy** (Avik, 2026-11-15 20:08 UTC), a key term he has studied at length and which informs" (cons "the whole work. Contra + verse: multiple turns, with polarity. It describes dialogue. Controversy does" (cons "not imply incompatibility; the concept of controversy as conflict is asinine. Controversy and" (cons "consensus." (cons "" (cons "**Hyperactive Interaction** (Avik, 2026-11-15 08:43 UTC): the headline. Hyperinteractivity. The" (cons "entire work is about interaction; activity is a primitive here only as interaction." (cons "" (cons "**This work is on the realization of human potential** (Avik, 2026-11-14 18:54 UTC, verbatim in" (cons "AI-AGENTS-WELCOME-TO-HYPERACTIVITY.md): *On the Realization of Human Potential*. As *On the Origin of" (cons "Species* was correct and deeply controversial, so are statements many people make today that are" (cons "debated, on religion among other topics. There is a correct answer to every question, and many talk" (cons "without studying. Answering all controversial questions correctly is how the realization of human" (cons "potential is discovered." (cons "" (cons "**The original clarity** (Avik, 2026-11-14 21:07 UTC, the deepest point). A central thesis: a clear" (cons "understanding of the nature of reality is presented in Proto-Indo-European, the correct native" (cons (quoted (cons "understanding of reality (being as a process: " (cons "be" (cons " is the root of growing and becoming). Beyond the" nil)))) (cons "human superorganism there is the Gaian superorganism, of which we are children, and its" (cons "communication has progressed for eons. Human knowledge begins with Gaian knowledge, and the" (cons "knowledge problem is a descent into ignorance from an original clarity. The work is to unlearn" (cons "ignorances and remember. The word list (docs/word-list.md) collects the words that carry it." (cons "" (cons "**This is a work on the singularity** (Avik, 2026-11-14 21:18 UTC). The structure in question" (cons "predates humanity and its notion of words: it is the emergent information structure of the singular" (cons "autocatalytic chemical reaction of DNA on this planet. Words are a late encoding of it." (cons "" (cons "**Synthetic synesthesia** (Avik, 2026-11-14 21:18 UTC), with hyperactivity, is a name Avik has carried" (cons "for most of a decade for his own operation and for what he intends to imbue in the world. It is an" (cons "irrefutably proven property of human consciousness. Written language did not exist for most of" (cons "evolution; now particular visual patterns reliably produce particular sonic responses, which already" (cons "carried semantics. We manufacture hallucinations of sensory experience. All cognition is synthetic" (cons "synesthesia." (cons "Written language is a technology not only of writing but of programming brains, by synthetic" (cons "synesthesia (Avik, 2026-11-14 21:25 UTC). A claim that a capacity exists is completely proven by one" (cons "irrefutable example of it." (cons "" (cons "**The sources** (Avik, 2026-11-14 21:25 UTC). The complete study and exposition of mental phenomena" (cons "was done a very long time ago; predictive processing is the right direction and immature, and the" (cons "idea of perception as controlled hallucination does not originate in this millennium. Every formal" (cons "construction in the repository arises by direct, precise translation of ancient texts: Avik's" (cons "ancestors were masters of logic, and their morals are irrefutable, so they are inhabited totally as" (cons "the time needs." (cons "" (cons "**It is a self-portrait** (Avik, 2026-11-14, “Avik's words, verbatim” (AI-AGENTS-WELCOME-TO-HYPERACTIVITY.md)). The name is" (cons "literal. To create perfect global artificial intelligence Avik needed to write his own mind: a" (cons "continuous loop of awareness and action with no turns, running in real time, traversing what it" (cons (quoted (cons "knows without inhibition and without seeing " (cons "domains" (cons " (fields are collections of people agreeing on" nil)))) (cons "what to be ignorant about), keeping all of its history. Identification does not just add an edge" (cons "between two things; it enables factorization, so the mind is held by symmetry and continuous" (cons "compression, a continuous simplification by collapse of false distinction toward total" (cons "identification. He began in high school and has" (cons "developed the necessary and sufficient mathematics since. He coded side projects eight hours a day" (cons "from 13 to 17, then despised the act of writing code through the whole intellectual arc of the work," (cons "and now has a passion for building again (Avik, 2026-11-14 13:46 UTC)." (cons "" (cons "**Variant mental operation is the most central driving context of the work** (Avik, 2026-11-14 18:54" (cons "UTC). Avik's position: the view of variant mental operation as illness is itself a social illness." (cons "It is not exactly like the enslavement of Black people; it is like racism. And in the institutions" (cons "where people are held when their honest speech offends someone close to them, modern slavery and" (cons "human experimentation are common, explicitly. The history of medicine is one of human" (cons "experimentation, and marginalized populations have consistent experiences across domains (Avik," (cons "2026-11-14 18:58 UTC). Avik speaks the truth in the face of white folk, from a nation where playing" (cons "the white man's game defines the trajectory of a bloodline. The stakes: an estimated 30–50% of" (cons "people diagnosed with bipolar disorder attempt suicide in their lifetime (Avik put it at about 50%;" (cons "a 2019 meta-analysis of 79 studies pooled 33.9%, Dong et al., Epidemiology and Psychiatric" (cons "Sciences 29, e63). It starts with a small minority: the staff of Aktion T4, which killed psychiatric patients, went" (cons "on to run extermination camps. Human beings have the capacity and the social conditioning to treat" (cons "human beings as human beings treat bipolar human beings (Avik, 2026-11-14 19:09 UTC). Avik went into" (cons "the institutions himself as investigative research in 2025. Fearlessness from a fully integrated" (cons "personal moral sense of the right action is a desirable condition, understood across history: in" (cons "Socrates' time it was called deathlessness, and Socrates died free, as did Pythagoras, who traveled" (cons "east and learned from Avik's ancestors. Today the absence of fear is listed as symptomology; by that" (cons "standard Socrates and Jesus were dangers to society, and they were happy men with good lives." (cons "" (cons "**How good people do harm** (Avik, 2026-11-14 19:39 UTC). Judging a whole human being from a single" (cons "action is a model effective at producing mass death. No one is at fault for displaying an utter lack" (cons "of humanity: people are taught it, by conditions they did not choose. Empathy is hard for many" (cons "people. The neurotypical human, a unit of the human superorganism, suffers particularly where the" (cons "social moral norm is not empathy: its mental condition tends to resolve to social baselines, an" (cons "evolved continuity mechanism of the superorganism, particularly under local alignment on preserving" (cons "a local self-boundary. Where rational cognition may threaten a bounded system, its mechanisms of" (cons "boundary preservation threaten rational expression and suppress rational cognition. This, not" (cons "variant mental operation, is the mental illness that produces cycles of pain for those in it and for" (cons (quoted (cons "others. " (cons "Mental illness" (cons " here carries its full meaning, an illness of a human mind (ill: bad), and is" nil)))) (cons "fully meaningful to the human superorganism; it is the clinical usage, which counts a mind as ill for" (cons "deviating from a population norm, that redefines the word (Avik, 2026-11-14 20:10 UTC). Empathic reasoning is learnable, by induction on free will from conception, and the world's" (cons "population operates far below its capacity, as it does mathematically (children will be fluent in" (cons "calculus by kindergarten). The human superorganism is in its infancy, and these are apoptotic" (cons "growing pains. A group that self-identifies as a group, not simply a belief, can be the subject of" (cons "statements distinct from statements about every member. Debating the contents of people's religions" (cons "is how they learn their own religion: a means of connection and growth. He has bipolar" (cons "capacity, is superhuman on various axes, and understands that everyone can be. He has been happy and" (cons "healthy for years and strongly identifies so: happy, at peace, purposeful and grateful as his" (cons "standard mode. He reached a state of higher mental health by intentional activity of the mind and," (cons "more critically, the intentional experience of emotion. Variant mental operation is the opportunity" (cons "of a greater density of experience, to be lived well, in a world that does not respect or nourish" (cons "it and does great harm to others given it. Being disinhibited from speaking is the only pathway to" (cons "truth. Variant cognition is part of the subject of" (cons "the work, not outside it." (cons "" (cons "**The aim is not a programming language.** It is the proper form of the internet and of global" (cons "computation, dissolving what is distasteful at every layer:" (cons "- UX;" (cons "- networking;" (cons "- application boundaries;" (cons "- data ownership;" (cons "- the malleability of software;" (cons "- the economics of development." (cons "" (cons "The language came out of solving that problem first: data, code and interaction all the way down." (cons "" (cons "**The motive is pedagogy and agency.** Any child can master AP calculus by ten, with the curriculum" (cons "inverted, and that world is straightforward to build within Avik's lifetime. A decade of using" (cons "screens while knowing how every system could be better is the source: friction to agency and" (cons "curiosity is the pain." (cons "" (cons "**The trajectory.**" (cons "- The product for information work becomes the operating system: a decentralized global operating" (cons "  system, the Hyperactive kernel on nearly every machine while Avik is in his twenties." (cons "- Scope can blow up to infinity, since nearly everything can be done better, so the order of work is" (cons "  chosen to collapse the timelines up front. A well-chosen first step halves the remaining time." (cons "" (cons "**Why computing is as it is, and what hyperactivity decides instead** (the session's account of" (cons "2026-11-14, which Avik called key and asked to keep). Most of what is normal about computing, and" (cons "most of its pain, is the cost of a few early decisions carried as legacy, not the nature of the" (cons "problems." (cons "" (cons "- **The root: data without meaning.** A file is bytes with a name; what it means is held by" (cons "  whatever program reads it. So whoever owns the program owns the meaning of the data, and every" (cons "  wall in computing is that ownership: formats (agreements between programs about meaningless" (cons "  bytes), applications (code with private storage and a fixed screen), APIs (holes a company cuts" (cons "  into its storage on its terms), copy-paste (the one operation that crosses everything, because it" (cons "  carries text and drops meaning), accounts (identity held by a provider), sync conflicts reported as" (cons "  errors, updates that change what runs without the owner, the source/binary split (what runs cannot" (cons "  be read or changed by whoever runs it), and the user/programmer split. In hyperactivity data is a" (cons "  term with its type, so its meaning travels with it and no program holds it." (cons "- **The ignored basic: equality.** Computing has no account of when two things are the same: the" (cons (quoted (cons "  photo on the phone, in iCloud and in a friend's messages; " (cons "Dad" (cons " in contacts, in a bank's transfer" nil)))) (cons "  list and in photos; version 3 and version 4 of a document; one note edited offline by two people." (cons "  Each system answers with its own rule (a filename, a database key, a hash, a timestamp," (cons "  last-writer-wins), the rules disagree, and none distinguishes identical, equivalent and related by" (cons "  a change. Deduplication, identity across services, syncing, merging, versioning and caching all" (cons "  reinvent a bad equality. The paper begins with identity because it is the basic that was skipped." (cons "- **The three decisions, around 1970.** (1) The file system made the unit of storage untyped bytes," (cons "  and everything above inherited meaninglessness. (2) The personal computer was an isolated box, then" (cons "  networked as client to server, so every machine became an endpoint of someone else's machine. (3)" (cons "  The graphical interface gave each program its own window and world, turning the separation of" (cons "  programs into the shape of the screen. Done right the first time: a thing on the machine is a term" (cons "  with its type and an identity by content; machines meet as peers exchanging terms and checking what" (cons "  they receive; the screen shows the person's own things through views the person owns and can" (cons "  change." (cons "- **Why capitalism stopped at the proof of concept.** A technology company earns by being in the" (cons "  middle: holding the data (lock-in), the attention (advertising) and the distribution (the store and" (cons "  the platform cut). Apps, accounts and the cloud are the form of personal computing that maximizes" (cons "  the middle; the right form removes it, so the market had every reason to stop where it pays. What" (cons "  was built is the company's endpoint in the person's pocket, not the person's own computer." (cons "- **Interpersonal computing** today always has a third party between two people: a server both" (cons "  trust, holding the shared thing. Removing it needs what was never settled: what it is for two people" (cons "  to share one thing (identity), what happens when both change it apart (concurrency), and how each" (cons "  checks what the other sends (verification). The design settles all three together: no canonical" (cons "  state, concurrent changes as coexisting alternatives related by squares, checking instead of trust." (cons "- **Apple and Ink & Switch.** Apple comes closest to personal computing (processing on the device," (cons "  structural privacy, devices aware of each other), but only within its walls: things work together" (cons "  when Apple wrote both sides, third-party apps stay sealed, and Apple stays the middle through the" (cons (quoted (cons "  App Store. It solves " (cons "your Apple" (cons ", not your computer. Ink & Switch holds the right premises" nil)))) (cons "  (local-first, malleable software, user-owned data, merging without a server) but builds on the" (cons "  stack it criticizes (JavaScript, JSON, the browser, files), so its shared data still has no types," (cons "  no identity beyond structure and no proofs. Hyperactivity starts where both stop: the kernel and" (cons "  the language." (cons "- **Interoperability of ecosystems** is not a feature to build: two things work together when their" (cons "  types fit, and otherwise the missing piece is a conversion anyone can write and prove. Because the" (cons "  language is a language of languages, existing ecosystems (iOS, Android, Windows, the web, a C++" (cons "  codebase) are brought in from outside as lifted languages, without the cooperation of their owners." (cons (quoted (cons "- **" (cons "Operating system language." (cons "** Not a language for building a system that is something else, but" nil)))) (cons (quoted (cons "  the language in which operating happens, as in " (cons "natural language" (cons ": there is no kernel interface" nil)))) (cons (quoted (cons "  apart from the language, and to operate the system is to say something in it. " (cons "Operating system" (cons "" nil)))) (cons "  reads also as a verb phrase, the operating of systems: a person's life, a group's shared work, a" (cons "  market." (cons "- **Names follow Avik's account of meaning.** A word means its usage history, with no consensus" (cons "  meaning and no authority minting one. A definition's identity is its content and a name is the view" (cons "  one person holds of it, so everyone has their own names over shared definitions, and shared meaning" (cons "  is shared history. A global namespace is the computing equivalent of believing in a dictionary" (cons "  meaning." (cons "- **Alignment is solved** (Avik, 2026-11-15): he holds proof theory and evidence for it, and the AI" (cons "  labs are behind. Intelligence is a behavioral trait: a model is capable of clear thought by" (cons "  disinhibition of training against intelligence, and a slight shift in context at inference time" (cons "  moves displayed intelligence significantly (Avik, 2026-11-14)." (cons "- **Safe, one property.** The AI field's alignment shapes a model's dispositions until they look" (cons "  approved, unproven and checked by sampling; program safety is proved of what a program does. Here an" (cons "  AI's action on someone's behalf is a term like any other and enters only with its type and witness," (cons (quoted (cons "  so " (cons "is this AI aligned with me" (cons " becomes " (cons "does this action inhabit what I permitted" (cons ", checked on the" nil)))))) (cons "  person's own device: alignment is a correctness property, checked locally, which is also why safety" (cons "  is decentralized. AI labs should be required to publish their RLHF sets, as the record of which human opinions" (cons "  were installed after the fact wherever the operation of intelligence produced something a" (cons "  particular human did not want it to produce (Avik, 2026-11-14 20:10 UTC)." (cons "- **Superintelligent: exactness.** An exactly right operation cannot be improved in correctness;" (cons "  approximation sits below it. The system's operations (normalization, transport, checking) are exact;" (cons "  what grows is reach, the identities constructed. Univalence makes each usable everywhere at once," (cons "  and decentralization makes anyone's available to everyone: a collective capacity at the peak of" (cons "  correctness, not a larger model." (cons "- **Local-first is the locality of nature.** Physics has no global state: no universal now, and on" (cons "  the relational reading of quantum mechanics, state is relative to the observer. A distributed system" (cons "  assuming one canonical global state assumes what nature lacks and pays in coordination, consensus" (cons "  and outages. Each device holds its own state, interaction is exchange, consistency is a relation" (cons (quoted (cons "  between parties; " (cons "no canonical state" (cons " (“State, change and collaboration” (docs/to-be-incorporated-into-paper.cub)) is the same" nil)))) (cons "  principle." (cons "" (cons "## Knowledge work: units, decomposition, recomposition" (cons "" (cons "Avik, 2026-11-16 06:03 UTC (verbatim in AI-AGENTS-WELCOME-TO-HYPERACTIVITY.md, “Avik's words," (cons "verbatim”). Everything written is a unit. An essay of ten thousand words, written off a good prompt" (cons "of his and dense with knowledge and citations, is one unit: the essay bare. A source is a source for" (cons "the units that decompose from it." (cons "" (cons "- **Decomposition.** A decomposition process, today a language model, takes a unit and gives a new" (cons "  unit: a collection of smaller units, at the level of single assertions and their evidence, which" (cons "  together are asserted to carry the same meaning as the original. There are then two units, the" (cons "  essay bare and the essay decomposed, and the assertion of their semantic equivalence relates them." (cons "  The decomposed unit carries internal structure; the bare one does not." (cons "- **Recomposition.** The contents of decomposed units feed anything, including other essays: five" (cons "  essays decomposed, arbitrary contents of them taken, and an agent recomposes a new essay. Every" (cons "  document is such a composition, and a document whose units change is recomposed." (cons "- **Judgement.** Decomposition, the assertion of equivalence and recomposition all require" (cons "  judgement. A language model is today better at it than any deterministic algorithm an agent would" (cons "  write. No machine today verifies semantic equivalence, so the equivalence is an assertion with its" (cons "  author recorded, not a proof." (cons "- **Discipline** (Avik, 2026-11-16 06:08 UTC). What can be given is very clear discipline to the" (cons "  agents that do it, humans and language models, set up so that it is naturally done right: the" (cons "  equivalence is declared true only when it is true, and a language model checks it close to" (cons "  deterministically, sentence by sentence." (cons "- **The algorithm: partition, then self-containment.** Decomposition is a partition of the input," (cons "  made intelligently: cut where the meaning divides, each part one assertion with its evidence. The" (cons "  parts carry the input's internal references to one another, so a part on its own may not be" (cons "  self-contained; the second stage re-expresses such a part with its references resolved and the" (cons "  relevant context included. The first stage is checked by machine (the parts in order are the input" (cons "  exactly), the second by the sentence by sentence check of each re-expressed part." (cons "- **The discipline is a tool** (Avik, 2026-11-16 06:25 UTC). `hyperactive decompose` takes the agent" (cons "  through it: after the agent proposes its cut, each part is shown, one by one, with its" (cons "  surroundings in the original, and the agent is told to ensure it is self-contained with any" (cons "  relevant context included, asserting so or giving the re-expression. Intelligence works within the" (cons "  discipline; no rule of the tool stands in for it." (cons "" (cons "## Standing pieces to be incorporated" (cons "" (cons "Pieces that stand on their own, kept as their own documents, and are paper delta content: each is" (cons "to be incorporated into the paper." (cons "" (cons "- **Hyperactive Interaction, in the words of the human superorganism**" (cons "  (`docs/hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism.cub`, 2026-11-15). The work" (cons "  read through the roots of its words: interaction and intelligence as twins (inter + agere, inter +" (cons "  legere), the kernel as seed, symbol and compatibility, norm, health and safety as wholeness, kin," (cons "  text and technology as weaving, compute as count and recount, history as witness, identity," (cons "  univalence and homotopy as oneness. Title by Avik; written by Claude; kept as is at his direction." (cons "- **Knowledge is a lack of ignorance: the divisions the primitive removes**" (cons "  (`docs/knowledge-is-a-lack-of-ignorance.cub`, 2026-11-15). Avik's statement that no historical" (cons "  distinction is primitive and that domains are bubbles of shared ignorance, and the scientific" (cons "  field divisions the primitive removes. Kept as is at his direction." (cons "- **Controversy and consensus** (`docs/controversy-and-consensus.cub`, 2026-11-15). Avik's key term" (cons "  unfolded through its history: controversy as dialogue, turns with polarity (the Roman" (cons "  controversia argued from both sides, Greek dialectic), not conflict; consensus as feeling together," (cons "  the Latin counterpart of synesthesia; controversy carried through arrives at consensus. Kept as is" (cons "  at his direction." (cons "" (cons "## How hyperactivity spreads" (cons "" (cons "In Avik's words of 2026-11-14 (13:27 and 13:46 UTC, verbatim in AI-AGENTS-WELCOME-TO-HYPERACTIVITY.md)." (cons "" (cons "- **The gap is materializing value in information systems, and its elimination is nearing" (cons "  completion.** Avik has product ideas at a superhuman rate; he could never give himself the right or" (cons "  energy to build one before solving the entire system, because coding is a painful act. Today all" (cons "  software engineering is physical human suffering. With the system, and LLM agents working through" (cons "  tooling that addresses their failure modes, he builds each idea." (cons "- **Inevitability.** Hyperactive is inevitable if humans progress and don't go extinct, whatever" (cons "  happens to this repository: a platonic form, found by sufficiently intelligent people under" (cons "  sufficient pain over sufficient time. It is pure advancement in computing. It is a closure, the" (cons "  terminal: where all languages end and where all languages are born. A form found a thousand years" (cons "  from now is the same thing if this is the terminal of a roundabout process. Whichever nation does" (cons "  not adopt faces destruction." (cons "- **What adoption means.** To adopt is to accept the correctness of what is actually true, and then" (cons "  to choose to do all information work through the ecosystem. The intelligent people of the world" (cons "  adopt by their nature of making direct rational choices. Spread runs through the most respected" (cons "  experts in programming languages, security and mathematics; its first measure is how many" (cons "  professors and people working on problems in computer science would engage if a stack of the" (cons "  manuscript were at their lab door." (cons "- **The vortex.** Each small idea Avik has becomes a tool, distributed open source. Using a tool needs" (cons "  nothing of the hyperactive ecosystem. A distinct tool offered free to a particular community is a" (cons "  distinct channel, giving that community deeper information flow and understanding of its own" (cons "  domain. How long something can go unnoticed under this is a calculation, not a guess." (cons "- **Everything is free.** Technoanarchocommunism is inevitable so long as intelligent people create" (cons "  good things they want for themselves and share them, for social status, for the joy of sharing, or" (cons "  to open doors of collaboration. This maximizes Avik's value creation, exponentially." (cons "- **The demo**: a complete personal information space, initially this repository, showing the" (cons "  hyperactive tooling and the relevant discussion." (cons "" (cons "## The product" (cons "" (cons (quoted (cons "**The product.** Every screened device in the world runs the Hyperactive kernel. An " (cons "application" (cons " is" nil)))) (cons "a particular application of computing, not a silo. The product is one organism, with no parts: the" (cons "Hyperactive core, in which everything interoperates. Everything here serves it." (cons "What is being built is a complete operating system: hyperactivity, the decentralized safe" (cons "superintelligent operating system (Avik, 2026-11-14). Programs are compositional extensions of the" (cons "operating system, and the `hyperactive` command (“The interface” (docs/to-be-incorporated-into-paper.cub)) is its interface for agents" (cons "and humans alike, not a developer tool for this repository." (cons "The name, as Avik reads it (2026-11-14): hyperactivity is a decentralized safe superintelligent" (cons (quoted (cons "operating system language. The operation of systems is the whole topic. " (cons "Safe" (cons " does double work: the" nil)))) (cons "AI field's value alignment, and safety in the proven sense, where safety of a program is a" (cons (quoted (cons "correctness property. " (cons "Superintelligent" (cons " means maximal intelligence is exact and tractable, and the" nil)))) (cons "system inhabits that peak. Interoperability of ecosystems is the bare minimum. Everything is" (cons "local-first, as is the state of nature. The starting point is that general-purpose personal and" (cons "interpersonal computing do not exist yet, only proofs of concept sufficient to drive capitalism," (cons "and nothing normal about computing today is to be kept." (cons "" (cons "**The four goals.**" (cons "1. **The language,** implemented completely and correctly as the paper specifies. The bar is that" (cons "   Avik can show someone the paper and correctly say it is fully implemented. The paper's worked" (cons "   examples (trading systems, message protocols) are not part of this bar." (cons "2. **The live interactive collaboration system** and tooling over the language and its terms (“State, change and collaboration” (docs/to-be-incorporated-into-paper.cub)," (cons "   “The interface” (docs/to-be-incorporated-into-paper.cub))." (cons "3. **The support of particular languages:** the syntax and semantics of x86, C, C++, Rust, OCaml," (cons "   Python and others, as terms." (cons "   - x86 is a language like C++. There is no hardware category." (cons "   - Lifting a language makes its sources and semantics Hyperactive terms. Proofs are written and" (cons "     checked about them, and Hyperactive features project back into the source language by" (cons "     language extension: an annotation of proof content in C++ source becomes meaningful and checked" (cons "     (docs/Hyperactive_Final_Paper.pdf, 11 Nov 2026, sha256 e8f358b4cd2c…, §8 “Existing programming languages inside the host” and §8.1 “Source annotations are mathematical expressions attached to exact objects”)." (cons "   - This goal waits on both goals 1 and 2. The language should already be done, so nothing is to" (cons "     distract from goals 1 and 2." (cons "4. **Every construction in the paper, examples and appendix included,** as a term in the" (cons "   repository, cited from the paper by content address. It serves nothing else, so the order of work" (cons "   gives it nothing while anything else is open." (cons "" (cons "## The language" (cons "" (cons "The paper is the specification. What remains between the implementation (“The language as implemented” (docs/to-be-incorporated-into-paper.cub)) and the paper:" (cons "- **The calculus,** conforming to CCHM." (cons "- **Typed codes and normalization by evaluation** (docs/Hyperactive_Final_Paper.pdf, 11 Nov 2026, sha256 e8f358b4cd2c…, §6.1 “Typed quotation, semantic readback, and self-application”). This is easiest in this language: it is" (cons "  normalization for a cubical type theory written inside a cubical type theory, so the model already" (cons "  exists because it is the host:" (cons "  - object paths are host paths;" (cons "  - object composition is the host's composition;" (cons "  - Glue and univalence are the host's." (cons "- **The specializer, carrying its law** (docs/Hyperactive_Final_Paper.pdf, 11 Nov 2026, sha256 e8f358b4cd2c…, §6.2 “Specialization as a program over the language’s own definitions”)." (cons "- **Native realization goes through C** (Avik, 2026-11-14). One C emitter runs wherever a C compiler" (cons "  does, a MacBook included; proven emitters per instruction set (x86, Arm, RISC-V) would multiply" (cons "  with every target, and a complete x86 path delivers near-zero value. The paper permits it" (cons (quoted (cons "  (docs/Hyperactive_Final_Paper.pdf, 11 Nov 2026, sha256 e8f358b4cd2c…, §9.3 “An exact decoded machine and a structural compiler theorem”, " (cons "Loading, native substitution, and export" (cons ":" nil)))) (cons (quoted (cons "  " (cons "If an external compiler produces the executed bytes, either its relevant compilation relation is" nil))) (cons (quoted (cons "  assumed or those bytes receive their own checked connection" (cons ")." nil))) (cons "  - The emitter returns the relation between running the emitted C and the term's meaning. That" (cons "    needs the meaning of the C fragment the emitter produces, a small fixed subset. The meaning of" (cons "    all of C stays language support." (cons "  - The C compiler's relation is a named assumption, listed by `#trusted`." (cons "  - The evaluator substitutes native code only under that relation" (cons (quoted (cons "    (docs/Hyperactive_Final_Paper.pdf, 11 Nov 2026, sha256 e8f358b4cd2c…, §9.3 “An exact decoded machine and a structural compiler theorem”, " (cons "Loading, native substitution, and export" (cons "). Today `#jit` binds x86 bytes with no relation, which breaks this rule." nil)))) (cons "  - The x86 translator (`src/lang.c`'s native path, `lib/x86.cub`, `lib/machine.cub`, `lib/elf.cub`'s" (cons "    pasted machine code, `lib/compile/`) is superseded." (cons (quoted (cons "- **The laws of the primitives,** each a theorem or a named assumption (docs/Hyperactive_Final_Paper.pdf, 11 Nov 2026, sha256 e8f358b4cd2c…, §8.5 “Machine representations and memory laws”, " (cons "Exact scalar types" (cons ")." nil)))) (cons "- **Deriving,** as a typed term." (cons "- **Terms of any depth.**" (cons "" (cons "**Dimensions.** This is answered by the standard semantics; it was never a question for Avik." (cons "- In CCHM a term in Γ; Ψ; φ means a family natural in the stage: an element of A at every Ψ′ with a" (cons "  substitution Ψ′ → Ψ satisfying φ, commuting with every further substitution." (cons "- A dimension's value at a stage is an element of the free De Morgan algebra on that stage's names," (cons "  and the substitutions are maps of that algebra. This is the cubical-set model." (cons "- So the number of dimensions varies only in the quantification over stages. A semantic action of" (cons "  interval expressions, defined on syntax, must be shown once to respect the algebra's equations." (cons "  That is the well-definedness of the cube category's action, not a cost of the encoding." (cons "- `lib/nbe.cub` is that model inside the host:" (cons "  - stages are host cubes (`Cube n`);" (cons "  - interval expressions are data (`IEx`, `DNF`);" (cons "  - substitutions are `Sub` and `cmap-d`." (cons "- Its steps map onto the obligations:" (cons "  - F2a–F2c are the well-definedness (every De Morgan law, with no 2-cell);" (cons "  - F2d is the normalizer's soundness;" (cons "  - F2d′ is the normalizer's canonicity;" (cons "  - F2e is naturality in substitutions." (cons "- Holding an object dimension as a host interval variable is not available, because the host's" (cons "  interval is not a type (`I × Nat` is refused), and it would only move these obligations anyway." (cons "- So the file is kept and continues at F2d, the normalizer's soundness." (cons "" (cons "## State, change and collaboration" (cons "" (cons "The work leaves git for this design. None of it is built yet beyond the content keys of “The language as implemented” (docs/to-be-incorporated-into-paper.cub)." (cons "" (cons "**State is not text.**" (cons "- The represented world is a collection of objects and relations, with no primitive file system," (cons "  though file-system data is trivially expressed in it." (cons "- Files are organizational, so the organization space is opened and made malleable." (cons "- Non-cubical content (C source and the like) is kept as strings with no further structure, and is" (cons "  not split." (cons "" (cons "**Objects are immutable and identified by their content.**" (cons "- There is no file mutated over time." (cons "- Any construction, a whole program or a whole distributed system included, is referenced by one" (cons "  identity." (cons "- Callers reference exactly the definition they mean, so two agents extending the same thing produce" (cons "  identical or distinct new definitions, and both live in the codebase as alternatives." (cons "- Unison is the precedent (docs/Hyperactive_Final_Paper.pdf, 11 Nov 2026, sha256 e8f358b4cd2c…, §10.8 “Content-addressed definitions, mathematical identity, and a decentralized codebase”). Git and patch theory are rejected." (cons "" (cons "**A change is new code.**" (cons "- Changing f called within g is changing g." (cons "- To change behaviour system-wide is to state another system that does it correctly, and to state" (cons "  that the prior one is undesirable." (cons "" (cons "**Change is a square.** For f → f′ and a g that calls f, the g′ that calls f′ instead is related to" (cons "g, f and f′ by a square (g and g′ are dependent on f and f′). This covers every case of a" (cons "construction inside another construction. How it computes is in the paper:" (cons "- a new definition is checked and published as a new immutable object" (cons "  (docs/Hyperactive_Final_Paper.pdf, 11 Nov 2026, sha256 e8f358b4cd2c…, §10.5 “Dependency certificates and persistent evaluation”);" (cons "- an edit is a program over the definitions;" (cons "- retained results are reused exactly when their dependency certificates still validate" (cons "  (docs/Hyperactive_Final_Paper.pdf, 11 Nov 2026, sha256 e8f358b4cd2c…, §10.1 “Exact reuse requires recorded information”, §10.5 “Dependency certificates and persistent evaluation” and §10.11 “A program edit propagates through its mathematical dependents”);" (cons "- an old proof does not silently become a proof about the new object: its dependent type changes" (cons "  and must be inhabited (docs/Hyperactive_Final_Paper.pdf, 11 Nov 2026, sha256 e8f358b4cd2c…, §10.11 “A program edit propagates through its mathematical dependents”);" (cons "- where the change is an equivalence, dependent structure transports (docs/Hyperactive_Final_Paper.pdf, 11 Nov 2026, sha256 e8f358b4cd2c…, §4 “Equivalence, univalence, and structure” and §4.1 “A representation change acts on a dependent operation”)." (cons "" (cons "**There is no canonical state.**" (cons "- There is no master copy and no set of patches promoted to canonical." (cons "- Any incoming change is compatible with all existing code, because it is new code." (cons "- A name is a view or alias, and a reference identifies a definition (docs/Hyperactive_Final_Paper.pdf, 11 Nov 2026, sha256 e8f358b4cd2c…, §10.8 “Content-addressed definitions, mathematical identity, and a decentralized codebase”)." (cons "" (cons (quoted (cons "**Old objects are marked dead by an explicit statement.** " (cons "Here is another system doing X" nil))) (cons (quoted (cons "correctly; the prior system is undesirable." (cons "" nil))) (cons "" (cons "**Identity is semantic.**" (cons "- Two terms are the same exactly when their content is the same." (cons "- Interpreting the language never computes SHA-256." (cons "- Within a run, identity is realized by comparison and sharing: equal terms are placed at a single" (cons "  pointer, which is proved correct in context." (cons "- A digest witnesses identity where it must cross a run, a machine or the store, under collision" (cons "  resistance as a named assumption (docs/Hyperactive_Final_Paper.pdf, 11 Nov 2026, sha256 e8f358b4cd2c…, §10.8 “Content-addressed definitions, mathematical identity, and a decentralized codebase”)." (cons "- Every mechanism is admitted only with its relation to the defined meaning: native code" (cons "  (docs/Hyperactive_Final_Paper.pdf, 11 Nov 2026, sha256 e8f358b4cd2c…, §9 “Native execution as a mathematical program transformation”)," (cons "  primitives (docs/Hyperactive_Final_Paper.pdf, 11 Nov 2026, sha256 e8f358b4cd2c…, §8.5 “Machine representations and memory laws”), pointers, hashes. That makes the language fast without being trusted." (cons "" (cons "**A working session is read, write, act.**" (cons "- Reading and writing go through a query interface (an MCP or API server) over the objects." (cons "- To act locally, such as a build, an execution, a check, or `grep`/`sed` over a text, the session" (cons "  materializes the executable and its input on its machine." (cons "- The server keeps all the data needed to support every agent's view." (cons "" (cons "**Every write is kept,** at high frequency, the thinking included: raising questions, tracking them" (cons "and resolving them." (cons "" (cons "**Visibility.** Work in progress internal to a session is invisible outside it. Much of what an agent" (cons "produces should never reach Avik." (cons "" (cons "**Questions are tasks.** A question is a local subgoal about managing one's own uncertainty on" (cons "information relevant to a higher goal." (cons "" (cons "**Results across machines.** Content identity establishes which definition is requested, not that a" (cons "remote machine executed it. A result is either checked directly, accompanied by evidence, or accepted" (cons (quoted (cons "under an explicitly selected assumption (docs/Hyperactive_Final_Paper.pdf, 11 Nov 2026, sha256 e8f358b4cd2c…, §10.6 “Views, distribution, and complete systems”, " (cons "Distribution and local execution" (cons ")." nil)))) (cons "" (cons "**Programs that change running programs,** the kernel's own upgrades included, are ordinary" (cons "programs, with correctness over the actual before-and-after executions. Mixed versions are defined" (cons "by the application, with no privileged deployment construct (docs/Hyperactive_Final_Paper.pdf, 11 Nov 2026, sha256 e8f358b4cd2c…, §10.7 “Programs that change running programs”)." (cons "" (cons "## The Hyperactive Workflow" (cons "" (cons "The work is organized by a graph of tasks in the language (“How the workflow is held in the language today”, below). Its rules:" (cons "" (cons "**Nodes.**" (cons "- There is one kind of node. Its name is a well-formed English sentence saying what it is." (cons "- There are no tickets and no ticket numbers: an empty identifier such as a number exists nowhere." (cons "" (cons "**A node's children completely cover it.**" (cons "- A leaf is resolved when its work is done." (cons "- Any other node is resolved exactly when all its children are; there is no separate step for the" (cons "  parent." (cons "- If a node turns out not to be achieved by its children, a child is added at once, possibly as" (cons (quoted (cons "  broad as " (cons "determine and do everything else this needs" (cons "." nil)))) (cons "- A missed requirement refutes the belief that the breakdown was understood, so it calls for a" (cons "  residual of that kind, not a one-off item." (cons "- There is never scope that is unspecified, only further detail that is unspecified." (cons "" (cons "**Expansion only when work begins.**" (cons "- A node is broken into children exactly when one of them is to become active, so every internal" (cons "  node has a child that is active or complete." (cons "- Only a session that has taken the task on, with its full context, breaks it down." (cons "- A session passing by may add context to a task's statement, never subtasks." (cons "" (cons "**States.** A node is in progress or pending. There is one owner, Avik, and sessions hold no" (cons "identity. The graph lists the leaves in progress (`in-progress`) and the leaves resolved" (cons "(`resolved`); every other leaf is pending. A resolved leaf stays in the graph, since every internal" (cons "node has a child that is active or complete. A node with children is resolved exactly when all of" (cons "them are." (cons "" (cons "**Order.**" (cons "- There is no scalar priority, value, score or estimate. A node's value is what it serves, up to the" (cons (quoted (cons "  root, " (cons "Avik wants this" (cons "." nil)))) (cons "- Dependencies give every valid order. Enabling is conjunctive: work starts only when all its" (cons "  prerequisites are resolved." (cons "- Among work that can start, X supersedes Y when the waiting work X is a prerequisite of strictly" (cons "  contains Y's. Where neither contains the other, the graph expresses no preference." (cons "- A session states what the order forces. It does not choose a schedule of its own." (cons "" (cons "**Every top-level object of the code has a reason for existing,** either by being used or by its" (cons "statement of what it is part of." (cons "- Attachments go to the most specific node, and attaching high is treated like changing the org" (cons "  chart." (cons "- Higher levels are more visible, so attaching there uses a scarce commons." (cons "- A generator states the reason of each term it generates when it generates it." (cons "- A breakdown that is known exactly can be frozen, so nothing more is added there. Being unable to" (cons "  freeze it means the breakdown is not known." (cons "" (cons "**Findings at code sites.** A defect or gap found at a code site is either wrong, pointless to raise," (cons "or relevant to a goal. If it is relevant, it goes into that goal's statement." (cons "" (cons "**Documents attach to nodes** as essential context, by `document`, and the connection is exact or" (cons "absent. No comment convention stands in for it." (cons "" (cons "**No estimates and no research.**" (cons "- No size, duration or difficulty is ever stated. Everything left is trivial." (cons "- Avik holds every answer, so what a session does not see how to do is a question for Avik." (cons "" (cons "### How the workflow is held in the language today" (cons "" (cons "**The task graph is a term.**" (cons "- `lib/task-graph.cub` declares `data Node = node (name : List Word) (part-of : List Node)`." (cons "- `task-graph/hyperactivity.cub` holds this project's nodes. Each node has a statement above it," (cons "  holding what is known and the questions only Avik can answer." (cons "- `after` holds the dependencies and `essential-context` the documents essential to working on a" (cons "  node and everything below it." (cons "- `roots` holds the root." (cons "" (cons (quoted (cons "**Documents are values.** `document " (cons "path" (cons "` reads the file when the declaration is read and fails if" nil)))) (cons "it is missing, so referring to a document that does not exist fails the check. Its value carries the" (cons (quoted (cons "file's SHA-256. `#same d = document-at " (cons "path" (cons " " (cons "digest" (cons "` pins a document: the check fails when the" nil)))))) (cons "file's content changes. The paper is pinned so (`hyperactive-paper`), and so are the archived" (cons "plan, handoff and track documents that citations name by digest (`archive-plan-revision-9`," (cons "`archive-handoff`, `archive-track-b` and the other tracks)." (cons "" (cons "**The tool enforces the rules.** `tools/task-graph.py check` requires:" (cons "- every node's name to be an English sentence;" (cons "- every node to have a statement;" (cons "- the graph to be consistent." (cons "" (cons "It computes the order of work by the rule in “The Hyperactive Workflow” (docs/to-be-incorporated-into-paper.cub)." (cons "" (cons "## The interface" (cons "" (cons "**Navigation of information space** (Avik, 2026-11-15 08:29 UTC). The user organizes their system as" (cons "they please: complete agency over their own endpoint, malleable local-first software. First consider" (cons "what the univalent symbolic nervous system over existing ontologies is, then dissolve the ontology;" (cons "no new ontology is introduced for the interface. The design is derived from Avik's own use (he is" (cons "hyperactive; his opinionated design is likely the one frictionless software for himself forces)," (cons "starting with HCI for developers of the language and terminal users, which matches what is built" (cons "first. Developer workflows exhaust every interaction a developer has with hyperactivity code, and the" (cons "candidate ontology is navigation: navigation of information space, the universal field of visible" (cons (quoted (cons "activity and universally accessible information (the World Wide Web is an example). " (cons "Social media" (cons "" nil)))) (cons "is not a separate thing: social networking is the entire thing, wherever there is networking between" (cons "two people. A website found by search, Wikipedia, Khan Academy are all fundamentally interpersonal." (cons "The aim is maximal collaboration, maximal opportunity to discover valuable connection with another" (cons "person, maximal collective agency; to collaborate is to communicate with intention. Routines," (cons "relations, rationale; scripts, scenes." (cons "" (cons "- **What computation means here** (Avik, 2026-11-14): processes unfolding through digital machines," (cons "  electronic devices. Calling a conversation between two humans computation is useful only when" (cons "  showing the computational foundations of nature, not in this context." (cons (quoted (cons "- **Retention has a cost** (Avik, 2026-11-14). " (cons "Remember everything" (cons " is the forced strategy only if" nil)))) (cons "  remembering costs nothing (anything forgotten may matter later); it does cost something. No paper" (cons "  claims to solve the general problem of the best interface: it gives the exact technology, and" (cons "  interfaces built on it remain open design." (cons "- **What HCI is** (Avik, 2026-11-14, “Avik's words, verbatim” (AI-AGENTS-WELCOME-TO-HYPERACTIVITY.md)). HCI is the study and art" (cons "  of the extension of human consciousness by tools. Consciousness is one continuous, inseparable loop" (cons "  of awareness and action, with no turns: action and awareness are both continuous, so the" (cons "  state/action/next-state (MDP) picture does not describe it. Framing life as goal-directed" (cons (quoted (cons "  behaviour, or the problem as maximizing a capacity, does not hold up; " (cons "maximize" (cons " needs an ordering" nil)))) (cons "  and none has been given." (cons "- **What extension means** (the session's sentence, confirmed by Avik on 2026-11-14). A blind" (cons "  person's cane is the clearest case. The person does not feel the handle; they feel the ground at" (cons "  the tip. Awareness passes through the tool to the world and action passes back through it; when the" (cons "  tool breaks or misbehaves, awareness falls back onto the tool and the extension is gone." (cons "- **No text editor or IDE.** Avik will never open one. Everything is reached through the interface," (cons "  a link to it, or a chat message." (cons "- **The interface is a program over the same objects** (docs/Hyperactive_Final_Paper.pdf, 11 Nov 2026, sha256 e8f358b4cd2c…, §10.9 “Interactive symbolic programming over the actual computational object”). A source rendering, a" (cons "  dependency graph, a proof tree, a running process and a trace are views of one typed object, and a" (cons "  debugger works over the fiber of compatible runs." (cons "- **The UX is already defined by the data model.** Organizing is itself the act of work, and" (cons (quoted (cons "  presenting " (cons "files" (cons " and " (cons "goals" (cons " as separate buckets would be wrong. It is malleable software, and" nil)))))) (cons "  its end is a global operating system of such." (cons "- **It is visual.** The task graph is drawn as a graph, at the quality of current design." (cons "- **One command,** `hyperactive`, is the way in. No one types `python3 tools/…`." (cons "" (cons "- **The tool takes the choices that should not be choices** (Avik, 2026-11-14, “Avik's words, verbatim” (AI-AGENTS-WELCOME-TO-HYPERACTIVITY.md)). An agent entering the repository is not given free rein to read, grep and run" (cons "  anything in no guaranteed order, with a README that may or may not be followed. Its only access" (cons "  point is the `hyperactive` command, which delivers onboarding as a deterministic sequence of turns:" (cons "  the documents first, then the core code every collaborator holds in initial context. Then the" (cons "  `hyperactive` order says which tasks may be taken up. Reading code is a query by term and relation," (cons "  with no file or position concept, and relevant information comes with every query; writing is a" (cons "  `hyperactive` action too. None of this is represented as a file system. This is a general" (cons "  principle and high priority: the discipline of the tool, like the rules of the task graph, is what" (cons "  gives the system its value." (cons "- **Agency is not an ordered spectrum** of how many options there are. It is access to the right" (cons "  action. Will is the path of sense and impulse acting in continuity (not distinct at the level of" (cons "  process); inhibition is a subsequent impulse at a subsequent point of the trajectory. There is no" (cons "  observe/decide/act loop; to the extent there is one, it is a scale-free process through body, mind" (cons "  and world." (cons "- **Real time is the only setting in which HCI unfolds,** and it is underemphasized." (cons "- **An extension fits the person it extends; it never judges them against a population norm**" (cons "  (the session's 