n `comp (λ i → A) (λ j → [ ... ]) a0`, transport" (cons "`transp (λ i → A) a`. Whether a λ or an application is a path's or a function's is decided by the" (cons "checker (below), so it is written the same way. `lib/std.cub` has `refl`, `sym`, `_∙_`, `cong`," (cons "`subst`, `transport`, `funExt`, equivalences and `ua`, with `calc` chains:" (cons "`calc a ≡ b by p ≡ c by q` (each step on its own indented line if long), composed by `_∙_`." (cons "" (cons "**Declarations.** A data type lists its constructors by fields (`cons (x : A) (xs : List A)`) or by" (cons "type (`cons : A → List A → List A`); a constructor whose type ends in `a ≡ b` is a path" (cons "constructor of a higher inductive type. A definition is a signature and equations; its equations" (cons "may match constructors at any depth, path constructors with their dimensions (`twist (loop i)`)," (cons "and implicit arguments as `{p}`. A codata type lists its fields (`codata Stream A where head : A;" (cons "tail : Stream A`), and a value of it is defined by copatterns: `(smap f s).head = f s.head`." (cons "`record R A = { f : A ; g : B }` is a Σ with named projections, and `R { f = a ; g = b }` (the" (cons "fields by name, in any order), `record { f = a ; g = b }` or `(a , b)` a value of it; `R { r | g = c }`" (cons "is `r` with the fields given replaced; `x.f` projects. `mutual` groups definitions that call each other;" (cons "`postulate x y` declares names without values." (cons "" (cons "**Recursion.** A call on a field of the matched argument is structural, applied to all its later" (cons "arguments or to fewer (a partial call is the function of the rest: `lapp (f k)` passes it); a definition at a type with" (cons "a clock recurses through any functions where a later value is expected (“Guarded recursion” in “The language as implemented” (docs/to-be-incorporated-into-paper.cub)). A call on a field's field," (cons "at any depth (`fib (suc (suc n)) = plus (fib n) (fib (suc n))`), is course-of-values: the sp