laration read so far, one line each: its position, the names it declares" (cons "(those generated from it included) and the positions of the declarations it mentions" (cons "(`tools/task-graph.py why` and `unexplained` read it). `CUBICAL_PROFILE=1` prints the run's profile, `=show` the profile from the last `#show`. The core forms the language compiles to" (cons "(`(lam x b)`, `(elim P e ((c x) b))`, …) are still read from files of other extensions, and" (cons "`--print FILE` prints such a file in the surface syntax." (cons "" (cons "### Rewrites see only the two cells involved" (cons "" (cons "Each cell has one principal port; a step rewrites two cells whose principal ports meet. No rule" (cons "consults an environment or context. Being under a face such as `i = 0` is a substitution of the" (cons "dimension by the endpoint. Applying a dimension binder puts a substitution cell on its body, and" (cons "that substitution re-activates exactly the stuck values it unblocks: `p @ i` under `i := 0` becomes" (cons "the left endpoint of `p`. The step count is fixed by the term: identical with any number of worker" (cons "threads. Reading a stored value" (cons "costs the same whether or not the value has arrived: a read that arrives first waits on the wire" (cons "and is served the same one-level copy, and waiting is not a step. Every reading is taken over the" (cons "complete normalization of what was posed. A worker locks the active pair and the cells it rewires," (cons "in address order, and revalidates before rewriting." (cons "" (cons "### Values include equality" (cons "" (cons "Besides functions, pairs and data, values are: the interval (`0`, `1`, dimensions, `~`, `/\`," (cons "`\/`, kept in normal form), paths (a value with a dimension abstracted), faces (conditions on" (cons "dimensions), partial values (systems), composition, Glue types and their elements, compositions" (cons "of types and their elements, and higher inductive types (data types with path constructors)." (cons "A constructor's field may be a path in the type itself, of any dimension (the truncations'" (cons "arguments: `squash (x y : T) (p q : x ≡ y) (i j : I)`); such a field is a map from the interval into" (cons "the type, so it is strictly positive, and the checker accepts it." (cons "" (cons "**Partial values.** `[ i = 0 ↦ a , i = 1 ↦ b ]` is a value defined only where its faces hold." (cons "Each branch is kept unbuilt, as syntax with its environment, and is built with its face's" (cons "substitution applied (`a` with `i := 0`) only when an operation reads it. If a substitution makes a" (cons "face true (here `i := 0`), the whole partial value becomes that branch." (cons "" (cons "**Composition.** `comp A u a0` takes a line of types `A(i)`, a starting element `a0 : A(0)` and a" (cons "partial value `u` (where it is given, what the result must be along the line), and produces an" (cons "element of `A(1)` matching `u`. Transport is composition with nothing given. How it is computed" (cons "depends on what kind of type `A(i)` is; each case is a term in `lib/prelude.cub`, not C:" (cons "- functions (`%comp-pi`): to apply the result to `x : A(1)`, move `x` back to each `A(i)`, apply," (cons "  and compose the results in the codomain;" (cons "- pairs (`%comp-sigma`): compose the first components, then the second components along the line" (cons "  the first one traced;" (cons "- paths (`%comp-path`): compose pointwise, adding the path's two endpoints to what is given;" (cons "- Glue (`%comp-glue`): this is where univalence computes, so transport along `ua e` applies `e`;" (cons "  on the end's faces the fibre over the composed base comes from the equivalence's contractibility;" (cons "- universes (`%comp-u`): a composition of types is a type of its own, `%hcompU A S` (Cubical Agda's" (cons "  `hcomp` in `Type`). Its faces `S` are the tube's lines of types from `A`, and the complement of" (cons "  the tube's face carries `A` itself, so where the tube is empty the composition is `A` and a" (cons "  closed composition of types is a type. Its elements are `glue` values; on a face, `%unglueU`" (cons "  transports back along that face's line. Composition through it (`%comp-gluel`) composes the" (cons "  unglued base and then, on the end's faces, takes the fibre of that transport over it from" (cons "  `%tproof`: the transport fillers along the line and one composition back along it. No" (cons "  equivalence and no contractibility proof is involved, so eliminating a higher inductive type" (cons "  into the universe and transporting through the result costs transports along the face lines," (cons "  at every nesting depth." (cons "" (cons "A `glue` value's base is held unbuilt. Where the system is total (on the end's faces of a" (cons "composition through a Glue type or a composition of types, the usual case) the value is the face's" (cons "element and the base is never read; built, it is a further composition whose tube carries the" (cons "fibre paths, and those compose generically one level down, so each level of nesting would pay for" (cons "every level below it." (cons "" (cons "**Data types.** One mechanism serves every declared data type, with nothing written per type:" (cons "- moving a constructor value along a line of data types (e.g. `List A(i)`) moves each of its" (cons "  fields along its field type; this is derived from the declaration;" (cons "- a path constructor such as `loop i` must still meet its declared endpoints after moving, so the" (cons "  result is corrected by a composition that glues those endpoints back on;" (cons "- composition is generalized (Cubical Agda's `gcomp`): the tube gets the complement of its face," (cons "  carrying the transported starting value. At every closed point the tube is then total, so a" (cons "  composition never leaves a formal composition behind where nothing was to be composed: a" (cons "  composition with an empty tube is transport, transport along a constant line of a closed type" (cons "  is the identity (`transp (λ i → S1) base` is `base`), and transport along `ua not` of `true` is" (cons "  `false`;" (cons "- in a data type without path constructors, a composition whose starting value and sides are" (cons "  all one constructor goes into the fields, each composed along its type at the earlier fields'" (cons "  fillers (CCHM's rule), so `λ j → comp Nat [ j = 0 ↦ 1 , j = 1 ↦ 1 ] 1` is `λ j → 1` and a path" (cons "  field transported along `ua` is a constant path again. The machine looks at the starting value" (cons "  and then at each side at a fresh dimension; a side that is not that constructor (a variable)" (cons "  keeps the composition formal, and a substitution decides again. The checker accepts a formal" (cons "  composition in such a type only when its tube covers every closed point, as the machine's own" (cons "  do, so a closed value of such a type is a constructor;" (cons "- a composition in a data type that cannot be computed further is kept as a value, `hcompD`; a case" (cons "  analysis meeting such a value applies itself to the pieces and composes the results in the" (cons "  result type." (cons "" (cons "### Work is done once, and only where it is read" (cons "" (cons "A shared subterm is held by a duplicating cell that copies lazily, one level at a time as it is" (cons "read. A stored value lives once, and readers copy its top cell. A substitution of dimensions is" (cons "recorded on the reference, not applied by copying. A subterm in a position that might not be read" (cons "is held unbuilt until an operation meets it: `fst (a , b)` never computes `b`, even if `b`" (cons "diverges. `delay e` holds `e` so wherever it stands: it has `e`'s type, an operation meeting it" (cons "builds it, `force` of it is it, and its code is `cthunk` (the first-order and C++ back ends," (cons "being strict, compute it where it stands). A λ's subterms that do not mention its variable are computed once, however often the λ is" (cons "applied. A case is one cell, and selecting a branch is one step." (cons "" (cons "Equal terms reached by different routes are also computed once. Every cell that will produce a" (cons "value (a thunk, a saturated call, an application of a known λ, a case) carries a key: its compiled" (cons "body over the keys of the values bound in it, interned, so one term is one pointer. A value's key" (cons "is its constructor over its parts' keys; a held value (a box) is named by what was put in it, and a" (cons "copy out of a box, a definition unfolded, and the scrutinee a case branch rebuilds from the fields" (cons "it took all carry that name, so one value has one name by whatever route it is reached. A producer" (cons "is pending on its key from its creation; when one fires while another of the same key is pending," (cons "its value goes into a box held by the entry, and the other reads the box instead of computing" (cons "(waiting on the wire, uncounted, if the value has not arrived). Retention is reachability: an" (cons "entry lives exactly while a producer is pending or a reader holds the box; the table holds nothing" (cons "on its own, and two boxes with equal values but different origins are not identified (a numeral" (cons "computed by `add` and the same numeral written out are two values). Naive Fibonacci shows it:" (cons "`fib (n+2)` demands `fib (n+1)`, which demands `fib n` while the outer `fib n`" (cons "is pending, so every `fib k` is computed once and the work is linear in the calls (unary addition" (cons "dominates the count), whether the argument is a numeral the machine computed or one written out." (cons "" (cons "Compiled code follows the same rule. Records (a λ's or thunk's body) and case tables are interned," (cons "so equal code compiled twice is one pointer, and the checker compiles every definition's quoted" (cons "code again at each reading. Between top-level forms the code is sorted by what still refers to it:" (cons "what a definition, a cell or kept code can build from is kept whole; what only keys name (a λ's" (cons "key is its record over its captures' keys) loses its body and keeps the hash and SHA-256 interning" (cons "compares, so equal code compiled later gets the same pointer and the body back, and the memo finds" (cons "what it found before; the rest is freed. Output and step counts are those of keeping everything" (cons "(`CUBICAL_NOSWEEP=1`); `CUBICAL_SWEEPALL=1` sorts after every form, `CUBICAL_MEMEND=1` reports" (cons "the split at exit." (cons "" (cons "A reading reports its steps, and with them the memo hits (values found instead of computed) and" (cons "the values shared. The steps are the work this reading did, given what earlier readings left held" (cons "and the order the rewrites ran in: a term's second reading can cost less than its first, and with" (cons "workers a reading can find a value shared that it would have computed alone. Without the memo" (cons "(`CUBICAL_NOMEMO=1`) the count is a property of the term, the same at any number of workers;" (cons "with the memo the answers are." (cons "" (cons "### Open terms normalize, with types" (cons "" (cons "A stuck computation is one with no rule to fire because the thing it inspects is unknown: `f x`" (cons "with `f` a variable, `case n ...` with `n` a variable, `p @ i` with `p` a path variable and `i` a" (cons "dimension variable. It is kept as a value (a neutral) holding its parts; reduction continues" (cons "everywhere else, including inside the branches of a stuck case. When a substitution later" (cons "supplies the unknown, it fires. A neutral's type is computed from the variable at its head along" (cons "the operations applied to it, and a stuck path's endpoints are read from that type." (cons "" (cons "A reading of a checked definition, or of `the T t`, is taken at its type: `quote` in" (cons "`lib/check.cub` reads the value as a code (`lib/code.cub`), applying a function to a fresh" (cons "variable of its domain, reading a pair by its projections and a path at a fresh dimension, and a" (cons "stuck elimination's branches at fresh fields typed by the constructor's telescope, at the motive." (cons "So `λ p → p 0` at `Path Nat zero zero → Nat` reads `λ x0 → zero`, and a variable of a Σ type" (cons "reads `(fst x0 , snd x0)`. Typed readings give full normal forms, except inside an" (cons "elimination written without a motive that is the head of a stuck term (applied, projected, or" (cons "eliminated), whose type is not known there; reached at a known type, its branches are read at that" (cons "type. A stuck word elimination carries no motive, so its branches are read without types: the" (cons "type `T = P w` it is quoted at does not determine an arbitrary motive `P`, so reading them at `T`" (cons "would be unsound (a motiveless case can be read at `T` because its motive is constant). The" (cons "code satisfies two laws: evaluating it (`eval-g`) gives a value" (cons "convertible with the original, and quoting that value gives the same code. A failure report" (cons "prints its types (expected and actual, a type that was eliminated) the same way." (cons "" (cons "`#same` of two terms, either of them a checked definition or `the T t`, reads both at that" (cons "one type, so equal values compare equal however they are written. Other readings (`#show` and" (cons "`#same` of any other terms) are taken without a type: under a binder," (cons "a variable's type is not known, so a path variable stays stuck at an endpoint and nothing is" (cons "η-expanded. `#same` compares two readings as text: on well-typed terms equal texts are equal" (cons "values; two readings can differ while their values are equal." (cons "" (cons "### Reflection: `%view`" (cons "" (cons "`(%view v)` turns the outermost form of a computed value into an ordinary data constructor in one" (cons "step, whose fields are the value's own parts: a Π type gives `(wpi A B)` with `A` the domain and" (cons "`B` the codomain as a function, a stuck application gives `(wapp f a T)`. A program cases on this" (cons "like any data, so a program in the language can examine a value's structure. What it sees is the" (cons "computed value, not the source text that produced it; a function shows only as `(wlam f)`." (cons "`(%var T)` and `(%dim)` make fresh variables, `(%dnf r)` gives an interval's or a face's clauses" (cons "as lists of literals, and `(%motive f)` an elimination's motive. The type checker (`lib/check.cub`) is written with" (cons "these and runs on this runtime, over the values the runtime already computed for each subterm:" (cons "there is no second evaluator, and checking a definition is running that program on it." (cons "" (cons "### Inputs" (cons "" (cons "`#input x` declares a definition without a value. An operation that needs `x`'s value (applying" (cons "it, a case on it, a projection) is held at exactly that point. Everything that does not depend on" (cons "`x` reduces fully, and the parts of a result that do not need `x` are produced. `#supply x = t`" (cons "connects the value, and the held operations proceed. Unlike a variable, an input is not computed" (cons "with symbolically: what depends on it waits for it." (cons "" (cons "### Coinduction" (cons "" (cons "`codata Orbit (A : Type) where here : A; next : Orbit A` declares a coinductive record type by" (cons "its fields. A field's type may mention the parameters, the earlier fields, and the type itself" (cons "strictly positively (at any parameters not mentioning it, under Π codomains and Σ components);" (cons "the checker checks this. A field applied to a value is its projection: `here o`, or `o.here`." (cons "" (cons "A value of a codata type is made by a copattern definition, a definition whose body is λs and" (cons "lines over a record:" (cons "" (cons "```" (cons "unfold : {A : Type} → (A → A) → A → Orbit A" (cons "(unfold f a).here = a" (cons "(unfold f a).next = unfold f (f a)" (cons "```" (cons "" (cons "Such a definition may call itself, and the definitions of a `mutual` group may call each" (cons "other. Its value is its stuck call: a neutral of its declared type, holding the definition and its" (cons "arguments. A projection unfolds the call once (the body applied to the same arguments, at the same" (cons "dimensions) and takes the field. Nothing else unfolds it: an application, a comparison, a reading," (cons "and a path application at 0 or 1, which reads the endpoint from the declared type as for any" (cons "neutral path. So a process that never ends is a finite value, an observation of depth n costs n" (cons "unfoldings, and a definition that is its own tail (`zeros`, whose `next` is `zeros`) is held as" (cons "its call. A record stands only as the body of a copattern definition." (cons "" (cons "The checker (`chk-codef` in `lib/check.cub`) requires every call of the group in a field's term to" (cons "be guarded: it is the head of the field's term (applied to arguments not mentioning the group, at" (cons "any dimensions), or stands there under a λ, a line, a pair, a constructor, a case or system" (cons "branch, or a let's body; never as an argument or eliminated. Every body of a group is found guarded" (cons "before any is checked, since checking one can unfold another. Each body is then checked at its" (cons "type, the group's calls at their declared types. A guarded call is productive, so the value exists at" (cons "every depth. At a path type the boundary is checked field by field (a record is compared with a" (cons "value by its fields), so it holds at every depth. Two stuck calls are convertible when their" (cons "definitions and arguments are; there is no η for codata, so two definitions whose unfoldings are" (cons "bisimilar are not convertible. Their equality is a path, and a path between two values of a" (cons "codata type is a bisimulation." (cons "" (cons "Composition in a codata type is a copattern definition generated from the declaration (`%comp-D`):" (cons "each field composed along its type, at the parameters' lines and each earlier field's filler. A" (cons "transported process is again a process, unfolded field by field when it is observed." (cons "" (cons "`#show t` reads a stuck call as the call. `#observe n t` reads it unfolded n levels deep, as" (cons "records. An unfolding is named by the call it unfolds, so two unfoldings of one call pending at" (cons "once share the body (“Work is done once, and only where it is read” in “The language as implemented” (docs/to-be-incorporated-into-paper.cub))." (cons "" (cons "### Guarded recursion" (cons "" (cons "```" (cons "nats : Stream κ Nat" (cons "nats = 0 ∷ smap suc nats" (cons "" (cons "fibs : Stream κ Nat" (cons "fibs = 0 ∷ 1 ∷ zipWith plus fibs (stail fibs)" (cons "" (cons "#same nth 10 (λ κ → fibs {κ}) = 55" (cons "```" (cons "" (cons "`▸ κ A` is an `A` one tick of the clock `κ` later: the Π type `(α : Tick κ) → A`. A tick is bound" (cons "by λ and given by application, and nothing else: `Clock` and `Tick κ` are the domains of Π types" (cons "only, in no universe, so a tick cannot be stored, returned, or let-bound. The checker's" (cons (quoted (cons "timelessness rule makes " (cons "later" (cons " mean later: in the body of a tick λ, a function applied to the" nil)))) (cons "tick α may use no variable bound at or after α. So `λ α → x α α` is rejected (one tick spent" (cons "twice) and `λ α β → x α β` accepted. Interval variables are exempt: `λ α (i : I) → p i α` turns a" (cons "path of later values into a later path, and `λ (i : I) α → p α i` turns it back. This is sound" (cons (quoted (cons "because the interval does not vary in time: the " (cons "earlier" (cons " of a context extended by an interval" nil)))) (cons "is the earlier context extended by the interval, ◁(Γ × I) ≅ ◁Γ × I, as in the cubical models of" (cons "guarded type theory." (cons "" (cons "`dfix : (▸ κ A → A) → ▸ κ A` (at every level: `next`, `⊛`, `dfix`, `fix`, `pfix` and `forceκ`" (cons "take `{l : Level}` first) is a stuck call of the kind copattern definitions make (“Coinduction” in “The language as implemented” (docs/to-be-incorporated-into-paper.cub)), with one" (cons "difference: it unfolds, `dfix f ⋄ = f (dfix f)`, only when applied to the tick constant `⋄`, and at" (cons "a tick variable it stays stuck. `fix f = f (dfix f)` is then the guarded fixed point, and every" (cons "recursion whose recursive use is under `▸` is well typed, whatever functions it passes through." (cons "`⋄` is not written in a checked term; it is the computation of `forceκ : ((κ : Clock) → ▸ κ (A κ))" (cons "→ (κ : Clock) → A κ`, a later value at every clock being a value now at every clock (the clock is" (cons "fresh, so its tick constant may be given). A total stream is a stream at every clock," (cons "`Str A = (κ : Clock) → Stream κ A`, observed through `forceκ` (`tl`, `nth`); `κ0` is the closed" (cons "clock. `pfix : dfix f ≡ next (fix f)` is the unfolding at a tick variable. It is a stuck call" (cons "too: at `⋄` both its ends are `fix f`, and it computes there, `pfix f i ⋄ = fix f` for every `i`" (cons "(the tick-unfolding definitions count path parameters among theirs). So transport along `pfix`" (cons "computes once `forceκ` gives the tick, and a guarded recursive type, a fixed point in the universe" (cons "such as `G κ = fix (λ X → Nat × ((α : Tick κ) → X α))`, can be unfolded and folded by transport" (cons "along `pfix` and still read canonical numerals. `pfix` being a path rather" (cons "than a judgmental equality is a property of the theory (`dfix f` at a tick variable must not" (cons "unfold, or normalization fails); the path computes wherever the equality would." (cons "Normalization terminates because the only unfolding fires on `⋄`, which only `forceκ` gives." (cons "" (cons "Guarded types are ordinary data whose recursive fields are later:" (cons "`data Stream (κ : Clock) A = _∷_ (head : A) (tail : ▸ κ (Stream κ A))`. Such a field is not a" (cons "recursive field (an elimination takes no hypothesis for it). Composition in `▸ κ A` is pointwise" (cons "(the composition of ticks and clocks is the identity), so transport along a line of stream types" (cons "moves each tail at its own tick, and the heads read are numerals again (composition with an empty" (cons "tube in a data type without path constructors goes into the fields, “Values include equality” in “The language as implemented” (docs/to-be-incorporated-into-paper.cub))." (cons "" (cons "The elaborator writes the ticks. A clock named in a signature (an argument of `Tick` or of a" (cons "data type's `Clock` parameter) is an implicit parameter. A definition with a clock whose" (cons "recursion is not structural is the guarded fixed point over its explicit parameters after the" (cons "clock. A term given where `▸ κ X` is expected and not itself later is a λ over a fresh tick, inside" (cons "which a later subterm standing where a present value is due is applied to that tick, and a" (cons "recursive call is the fixed point's self at the outermost such tick. A tick λ written by hand" (cons "(`1 ∷ λ α → ones`) is treated the same way, and so is the later component of a pair. A clock" (cons "given to a defined family (`G κ` with `G : Clock → Type`) is bound as well. A clock argument nothing" (cons "determines is the one clock in scope. A recursive call needed now is reported where it stands:" (cons (quoted (cons "`bad = smap suc bad` is rejected with " (cons "a recursive call needed now, not under ▸" (cons "." nil)))) (cons "" (cons "### Programs about programs, and the compiler" (cons "" (cons "Programs about programs are definitions over codes (`lib/code.cub`), and their outputs carry" (cons "paths, so a wrong one produces output that does not check. **`lib/match.cub`** (first-order" (cons "matching and rewriting over codes, capture-safe under binders; each rewrite step's path is the" (cons "theorem's instance in context), **`lib/rules.cub`** (the store's theorems as rewrite rules read" (cons "from their types), **`lib/nav.cub`** and **`lib/cost.cub`** (navigation over established" (cons "identities), **`lib/specialize.cub`** (normalize with held definitions abstracted, then rewrite" (cons "along the rules under a terminating discipline, composing the steps' paths), **`lib/derive.cub`**" (cons "(decidable equality as a code read off the data table), the certificate checkers (`lib/lin.cub`," (cons "`lib/linproof.cub`, `lib/eqproof.cub`, `lib/ring.cub`, `lib/intproof.cub`: search unverified, the" (cons "verdict decided by the checker), and `lib/autodiff.cub`'s typed theorems." (cons "" (cons "**The compiler.** `#jit f` compiles a checked definition to x86-64 and binds `f` to the bytes:" (cons "" (cons "```" (cons "plusN : Nat → Nat → Nat" (cons "plusN a b = case a return (λ k → Nat) of" (cons "  zero → b" (cons "  suc k → suc (rec k)" (cons "#jit plusN" (cons "-- ok: jit plusN   [250 bytes, the checker's conversion, 15744 steps]" (cons "```" (cons "" (cons "The checker's code for `f` is specialized (`lib/specialize.cub`), the result is accepted by the" (cons "checker as `f` (its conversion with `f`, or with `#jit f using t…` the path along the theorems" (cons "`t`, checked as the definition `f·jit`), and only then encoded by fixed templates" (cons "(`lib/machine.cub` decides the fragment, `lib/x86.cub` encodes) and mapped executable. A" (cons "definition outside the fragment (dimensions, composition, higher constructors, types at run" (cons "time) is reported with the reason and stays on the net. A call whose arguments are values of" (cons "the parameter types runs the bytes; any other call, and a `Word` result past 2⁶⁴ (the overflow" (cons "exit: compiled code is pure, so the net recomputes the call), runs `f` on the net. The" (cons "acceptance workloads are `experiments/jit/workloads.cub`. Only the specialized code" (cons "is checked against `f`; the translation to bytes after it, its passes and templates and the" (cons "boundary's marshaling, is trusted and carries no relation to the code (the Known facts in the task graph's goal statements, “The language” (docs/to-be-incorporated-into-paper.cub))." nil)))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
